[strategy/guidance/application/design-tokens/GUID-APP-UI-001-design-tokens-theming-guidance.md#layer-2--semantic-tokens]

#### Layer 2 — Semantic Tokens

Semantic tokens map primitive values to their role in the UI. **These are the tokens modules and utility classes reference.** Defined in `core-theme.css` on `:root` (default light) with `.theme-light` and `.theme-dark` overrides.

```css
/* core-theme.css — Semantic tokens (excerpt; default light mode) */
:root:not(.theme-dark):not(.theme-light),
.theme-light {
  /* Text */
  --text-primary:            var(--gainwell-soft-black);
  --text-secondary:          var(--neutral-600);
  --text-inverse:            var(--neutral-0);
  --text-error:              var(--red-500);
  --text-success:            var(--green-600);
  --text-accent:             var(--gainwell-aqua-green);

  /* Surfaces */
  --background-primary:      var(--neutral-0);
  --background-secondary:    var(--neutral-300);
  --background-accent:       var(--gainwell-aqua-green);

  /* Buttons */
  --button-bg-primary:       var(--blue-400);
  --button-bg-primary-hover: var(--blue-500);

  /* Widgets (form inputs, dropdowns) */
  --widget-border:           0.1rem solid var(--neutral-600);
  --widget-focus-outline:    0.2rem solid var(--pink-400);
  --widget-error-border:     0.1rem solid var(--red-500);
  --widget-bg-color:         var(--neutral-0);

  /* Icons */
  --icon-color-primary:      var(--blue-400);
  --icon-color-error:        var(--red-500);

  /* Tables */
  --table-bg:                var(--neutral-0);
  --table-alt-bg:            var(--neutral-100);
  --table-border:            0.1rem solid var(--neutral-600);
}
```

