[strategy/guidance/application/design-tokens/GUID-APP-UI-001-design-tokens-theming-guidance.md#layer-3--component-sizing-constants-and-dark-mode-override]

#### Layer 3 — Component-Sizing Constants and Dark Mode Override

Sizing constants (`--widget-input-height`, `--font-size-regular`, `--spacing-md`, etc.) are theme-invariant and defined on `:root`. Dark mode swaps only the semantic color tokens via `.theme-dark`:

```css
/* core-theme.css — Dark mode semantic overrides (excerpt) */
.theme-dark {
  --text-primary:            var(--neutral-0);
  --text-secondary:          var(--neutral-300);
  --text-error:              var(--red-300);
  --background-primary:      var(--gainwell-soft-black);
  --background-secondary:    var(--neutral-500);
  --button-bg-primary:       var(--blue-200);
  --widget-bg-color:         var(--gainwell-soft-black);
  --table-bg:                var(--gainwell-soft-black);
  --table-alt-bg:            var(--neutral-400);
}
```

All module CSS inherits light or dark automatically — no module-level theme switching code required.

