### Tenant Brand Extension Points

For multi-tenant deployments, tenant-specific brand tokens override only the semantic tokens that carry brand meaning. This is the mechanism described in PTN-APP-MTN-013:

```css
/* Tenant override — applied dynamically from the Tenant Theme Registry */
/* Only brand-relevant tokens are overridden; structural tokens remain shared */
[data-tenant="state-agency-example"] {
  --primary:          210 84% 38%;   /* Agency primary blue — must meet 4.5:1 on white */
  --primary-foreground: 0 0% 100%;
  --ring:             210 84% 38%;
}
```

```typescript
// src/providers/tenant-theme-provider.tsx
'use client';

import { useEffect } from 'react';

type TenantTokens = Record<string, string>;

export function TenantThemeProvider({
  tenantId,
  tokens,
  children,
}: {
  tenantId: string;
  tokens: TenantTokens;
  children: React.ReactNode;
}) {
  useEffect(() => {
    const root = document.documentElement;
    // Apply tenant tokens as CSS custom properties on :root
    Object.entries(tokens).forEach(([key, value]) => {
      root.style.setProperty(key, value);
    });

    return () => {
      // Clean up when tenant changes
      Object.keys(tokens).forEach((key) => {
        root.style.removeProperty(key);
      });
    };
  }, [tenantId, tokens]);

  return <>{children}</>;
}
```

